<title>USA: St Joseph hogs up $2.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs up $2.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Friday, barrows and gilts were $2.50 higher. Top $50.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>Interior Iowa moved 98,000 hogs Friday and 15,000 on Saturday. Packers needs increase and reports of possible</p>
<p>Taiwan purchases, hog prices jumped higher.</p>
<p>    US 1-3	230-270 lbs    49.50-50.00</p>
<p>    US 2-3	270-290 lbs    48.00-49.00</p>
<p>    US 2-4	290-310 lbs    46.50-47.00</p>
<p>Sows - no comparison. Top $50.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2	300-450 lbs    44.00</p>
<p>		    450-500 lbs    46.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3	500-550 lbs    48.00</p>
<p>		    550-700 lbs    49.00-50.00</p>
<p>    Boars:	300-700 lbs    41.00</p>
<p>		    200-300 lbs    42.00</p>
</text>
